/*!
\page page_stfgtpoint StFgtPoint

\brief Reconstructed 2D space point in the FGT formed by pairing an R-strip and a phi-strip hit.

\section fgtpoint_overview Overview

StFgtPoint is a 2D space point in the **Forward GEM Tracker (FGT)** formed by pairing
one R-strip hit (StFgtHit with layer 'R') with one phi-strip hit (layer 'P') on the
same disc and quadrant.  Construction failure (null inputs, mismatched disc/quadrant,
same-layer pair) sets \c mKey = −999; callers must verify \c getKey() != -999.

**Detector**: Forward GEM Tracker (FGT)  
**Stage**: 1D hit pairing → 2D space point

\section fgtpoint_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StHit → StFgtPoint
\endcode

Stored in the FGT point container within \c StFgtCollection.

\section fgtpoint_members Data Members

| Type | Member | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| \c Int_t | \c mKey | Unique point ID; −999 = construction error |
| \c Float_t | \c mChargeAsymmetry | (Q_phi − Q_r) / (Q_phi + Q_r) |
| \c Int_t | \c mRank | Quality rank for candidate ordering |
| \c StFgtHit* | \c mHitR | Associated R-strip cluster (transient) |
| \c StFgtHit* | \c mHitPhi | Associated phi-strip cluster (transient) |

The combined charge \c mCharge (inherited from StHit) = Q_r + Q_phi.

\section fgtpoint_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c getKey() | Unique ID (−999 = invalid) |
| \c getDisc() | FGT disc index (0–5) |
| \c getQuad() | Quadrant index (0–3) |
| \c getPositionR() | Radial position r (cm) |
| \c getPositionPhi() | Azimuthal angle φ (rad) |
| \c charge() | Combined cluster charge |
| \c getChargeAsymmetry() | Phi/r charge asymmetry |
| \c getRank() | Quality rank |
| \c getHitR(), \c getHitPhi() | Pointers to the 1D cluster hits |

\section fgtpoint_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StFgtPoint* pt = ptColl->point(ip);
if (pt->getKey() == -999) continue;  // invalid
float r   = pt->getPositionR();      // radial (cm)
float phi = pt->getPositionPhi();    // azimuthal (rad)
float x   = r * cos(phi);
float y   = r * sin(phi);
\endcode

\see StFgtHit, StFgtStrip, StFgtCollection
*/
